<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH PVT POSTS CZK 16 MLN 1996 NET LOSS.</title>
<headline>CZECH PVT POSTS CZK 16 MLN 1996 NET LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech software and data processing company PVT a.s. said on Thursday it posted an audited net loss of 16 million crowns for 1996, after a 532 million net profit in the previous year.</p>
<p> Net result (CZK mln)	15.99 loss   vs     532.45 profit</p>
<p> Gross result		  15.28 loss   vs     753.50 profit</p>
<p> Operating result	    41.50 loss   vs     742.71 profit</p>
<p> Production		 1,249.33	  vs   2,134.56</p>
<p>Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services	     1,639.08	  vs   2,483.22</p>
<p> Total assets	     2,011.11	  vs   2,414.55</p>
<p> Basic capital		784.04	  vs     784.04</p>
<p>Note. The results were calculated and audited according to</p>
<p>Czech accounting standards. PVT shares are traded on the main</p>
<p>market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
